l":"https://www.meetup.com/global-tongue-masters-language-exchange-social/events/316673331/","description":"We are hosting a relaxed watercolor painting session for our language exchange community here in Toronto. This is a chance to step away from our usual conversation practice and try something creative together. We will have basic supplies on hand, and the goal is simply to play with colors and enjoy the process in a low-pressure environment. You do not need to be an artist to join; it is just a nice way to unwind and connect with others in the group while we work on our paintings.\n\nThe session is open to anyone in the Global Tongue Masters community who wants to spend a couple of hours focusing on something visual. Whether you are looking to practice a new language while you paint or you just want a quiet space to meet some familiar faces, you are very welcome to attend. We will be set up to chat comfortably as we work, so expect a friendly, informal atmosphere.\n\nIf you are interested in joining us for this afternoon of creativity, please take a moment to RSVP so we can make sure we have enough materials for everyone. We look forward to seeing you there.","startDate":"2026-10-29T19:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"JJHW+4R Toronto","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"JJHW+4R Toronto, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Global Tongue Masters Language Exchange Social","url":"https://www.meetup.com/global-tongue-masters-language-exchange-social/"},"performer":"Global Tongue Masters Language Exchange Social"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Oct 2026 Toronto IAM Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-iam-community/events/316692895/","description":"Hi Everyone,\n\nSave the date for the next Toronto IAM Community Meetup on Oct 29.\n\nPls ensure you register at this form: (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfUzr-J6BRilxNXh7fq4ktl4V3eHhjgIXReIC5EVVyw90BqTQ/viewform?usp=publish-editor\n\nOnly attendees registered via the google form: (form removed as registration is now closed) will be admitted into the venue. Registration deadline is Oct 23, 2026 at 5pm Est.\n\nAGENDA\n**5:30pm -** Doors open\n**5:45pm -** Welcome by Toronto IAM\n**6:00pm -** Talk #1: TBA Mandate: What Security Leaders Need to Know.\n**6:40pm -** Break\n**6:50 pm -** Panel TBA\n**7:30pm -** Networking and social\n**8pm -** Event and attendees exit venue\n\nHave a great day,\nAn","startDate":"2026-10-29T21:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Accenture","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"40 King Street West, 30th FL, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto IAM  Community","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-iam-community/"},"performer":"Toronto IAM  Community"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Board Game Night!!!!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/geekzunited/events/316231714/","description":"Hello Meeples!!!!\n\nI host board game night every Thursday at Face to Face Games, located at 1398 Danforth Ave (about a 3 min walk from Greenwood station, or a 7 min walk from Coxwell station)! How it works I’ll be seated at the table at the very back right hand corner of Face to Face Games (near the washrooms).\n\nWe usually have 2 tables reserved for our group. (If you can’t find us, ask one of the staff members.) I’ll bring a variety of games from my own collection to board game night, but attendees are free to bring any of their own games as well! Got a brand new game you’ve been dying to play but never have enough players? Bring it along!\n\nGot a retro game that you think is a hidden gem? Bring it along and spread the joy! I usually come early at around 4:30pm. If there are other attendees who also arrive early, then we can play some shorter games until 6pm. Six o’clock is when the event officially starts and is when most attendees start trickling in.\n\nOnce we have most people assembled, we collectively decide which games we want to play and split into groups accordingly. We usually have one group tackling a heavy board game (ie. a game that tends to be more complex and takes longer to finish) while the others play short to medium-length games, but this is very flexible and will depend on turnout and the kinds of games people bring.\n\nIf you can only get here later or if you arrive late, don’t fret. We’ll see what game you can join so that you can get playing as soon as possible!\n\nRules of the Tables:\n\nWe are a cool and relaxed group - we swear! But to ensure things run smoothly and that everyone is having fun, we do some some rules we would like attendees to follow:\n\n\\- Please be respectful of people’s games and property\\. For example\\, if you’re having a snack \\(please share\\!\\)\\, make sure your fingers are clean before you handle cards\\, mats\\, meeples\\, and the like\\. People are generous to bring their games to board game night\\, so we want to be mindful not to damage or dirty their stuff\\.\n\n\\- Please be mindful of your cellphone usage during the game\\. Of course this doesn’t mean you can’t use your cellphone to shoot a quick text message or to check something quickly\\. we’re not monsters\\!\n\n\\- However\\, if you’re always focused on your cellphone \\(for example\\, watching a video or playing a cellphone game\\) and are not paying attention to the rules being explained\\, or you constantly need the other players to repeat themselves as to what sick moves they just made\\, then it ends up taking away from everyone’s enjoyment of the game\\.\n\n\\- Please be decent\\, in dress and in conduct\\. No bullying\\, excessive swearing\\, racist or sexist language\\, and all the other bad stuff\\.","startDate":"2026-10-29T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Face to Face Games","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1398 Danforth Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Geekz United","url":"https://www.meetup.com/geekzunited/"},"performer":"Geekz United"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"EmpowerHer Luncheon","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ladiespowergta/events/316256831/","description":"Join us for an inspiring evening at our EmpowerHer dinner, a networking business event dedicated to bringing together ambitious women who are eager to make meaningful connections and share their professional journeys.\n\n🌟 Where: Downtownn Toronto (venue to be confirmed)\n🕒 When: last Thursday of the monthth, 6pm -8pm\n👗 Dress Code: Business Casual - Show off your style!\nCost: 5$ to ensure attendance and prevent no shows\n\nEvent Highlights:\n\nMeet & Greet: Start the event with a warm welcome and casual introductions.\n\nDinner: Enjoy a curated menu of delicious cuisine as you engage in thoughtful discussions about business, life, and aspirations.\n\nInteractive Sessions: Participate in round-table discussions and ice-breaker activities designed to foster connections and collaboration.\n\nTakeaways: Leave inspired and with new contacts that could lead to your next big opportunity.\n\nWhy You Should Attend:\n\nExpand Your Network: Connect with professionals across various industries.\n\nShare Your Story: Every journey is unique, and yours is worth sharing.\n\nFind Your Tribe: Build supportive relationships that last beyond the event.\n\nRSVP Now to secure your spot at this empowering gathering. We can’t wait to meet you and witness the amazing connections that will unfold!","startDate":"2026-10-29T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"DOWNTOWN","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"downtown, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Ladies Empowerment Circle Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ladiespowergta/"},"performer":"Toronto Ladies Empowerment Circle Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"French at the Royal Conservatory","url":"https://www.meetup.com/diskuto/events/316624449/","description":"Join us for an evening of French conversation at B Espresso Bar in the atrium of the Toronto Royal Conservatory of Music (near St. George station)! We welcome all levels of French, and it's free\\*. Venez pratiquer votre français!\n\n\\*While there is no fee to attend this event, guests are expected to purchase something from B Espresso Bar, in accordance with RCM's restrictions on usage of the cafe atrium space.\n\n**Building location:**\nThe Royal Conservatory is at 273 Bloor St W, between Varsity Stadium and the Royal Ontario Museum (ROM). There are entrances off Bloor St. and Philosopher's Walk. If you enter from Bloor St through the large glass doors, follow the hallway on the left beside the staircase and turn left at the end. (Closest TTC: St. George)\n\n**Notes and restrictions:**\nThe host may or may not attend this event. Attendees are encouraged to seat themselves at two or more adjacent tables, as needed. Please form groups of 6 people at each table; do not rearrange chairs and tables to accommodate more people, as this obstructs the narrow walking space. Guests are expected to order something from the cafe, and are asked to please refrain from bringing outside food or drink. Attendees must leave the building at 8pm when the cafe stops serving.\n\n**Contributions:**\nIf you are a regular with us and would like to support the group, please send any contributions by e-transfer to [diskutomeetup@gmail.com.](http://diskutomeetup@gmail.com.) The yearly donation goal and amounts received year-to-date will be tracked anonymously on [this google sheet](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/18GfqYsis8Cf2XGg4KsKQJsY_0Fv3bsSQHwJAxvC1Km8/edit?usp=sharing). Thank you so much for your support.","startDate":"2026-10-29T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Royal Conservatory of Music","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Diskuto - Talk with Language Lovers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/diskuto/"},"performer":"Diskuto - Talk with Language Lovers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Nightmares — A Halloween Party With Something to Talk About","url":"https://www.meetup.com/social-events-toronto-30-head-out-toronto/events/316668635/","description":"**Haven’t been to a Halloween party in years?**\nMaybe it’s time.\n\n**A Halloween party with something to talk about.**\n\n*It’s in the Cards: Nightmares* is a Halloween social for people in their 30s, 40s & beyond, inside Moonlight Lounge (with secret alleyway access!).\n\nComing alone works well here. Everyone receives an outlandish nightmare scenario, then meets other guests while comparing and trading cards. Form a team of four for the rankings reveal and a chance to win prizes.\n\nIt's easy to start talking; the cards give you an easy reason to start a conversation.\n\nThis is a social event, not a dating or networking event. Costumes are encouraged, but optional.\n\n**Tickets:** $25 Regular · $35 Final Week\nAppetizers included. Refunds available until seven days before the event.\n\n**October 29 · 6:30–10:00 PM**\n**Moonlight Lounge · Toronto**","startDate":"2026-10-29T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"319 Augusta Avenue","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"319 Augusta Ave, Toronto, ON M5T 1N9, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Head Out Toronto: Social Events for 30s & 40s","url":"https://www.meetup.com/social-events-toronto-30-head-out-toronto/"},"performer":"Head Out Toronto: Social Events for 30s & 40s"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"👻 Ghost Tour of Old Toronto🌙!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/no-such-thing-as-bad-weather/events/316201022/","description":"# 👻 Ghost Tour of Old Toronto 🌙\n\n### Haunted Hotels, Dark History & The Ghosts of Downtown\n\nToronto has a long history — and some of it is considerably darker than the history books make it sound.\n\nJoin us for an evening walk through **Old Toronto**, where we'll uncover stories of haunted hotels, gruesome executions, mysterious deaths, and some of the stranger legends that have become part of the city's history.\nWe'll walk through the downtown core as the city settles into the evening, stopping along the way for stories about the ghosts, tragedies, and unusual events connected to the streets and buildings around us.\nAnd yes, we'll even explore **why Toronto has a long-standing fear of clowns.** 🤡👻\n\nThis isn't simply a walk through downtown.\nIt's a **curated storytelling experience** that looks at some of Toronto's history from a decidedly darker perspective.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 👻 What We'll Explore\n\nWe'll begin outside the **Royal York Hotel** and make our way through Old Toronto toward the **Hockey Hall of Fame**.\nAlong the way, we'll hear stories about:\n\n* 🤡 **Why Toronto doesn't like clowns**\n* 🏨 **The ghosts of downtown's historic hotels**\n* 💀 **Gruesome executions and forgotten tragedies**\n* 🔫 **A deadly reminder of why you should never play with guns**\n* 👻 **Restless spirits and strange encounters**\n* 🕯️ And much, much more…\n\nWe'll remain outside throughout the experience and **will not be entering the buildings**.\n\n***\n\n## 🕯️ A Little About the Experience\n\nThis is one of our **curated ghost walks**, rather than a regular social walk.\nI've researched the stories, developed the route, and brought together some of the stranger pieces of Toronto's history to create an evening experience that is part history, part ghost story, and part “what the hell happened here?”\nYou don't have to believe in ghosts.\n**You just have to enjoy a good story.** 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** In front of the **Royal York Hotel**\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **6:30 PM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes**.\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🚶‍♂️ **Pace:** Steady walking pace\n🏁 **End Point:** **Hockey Hall of Fame**\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$10 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis is a **curated ghost-walking experience**, rather than one of our regular social walks. The route, stories, and history have been researched and brought together specifically for this experience.\nThe fee helps support the time and work that goes into creating these walks.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🧥 Weather-appropriate clothing\n💧 Water\n📱 Your phone for photos\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis experience is great for:\n\n* 👻 People who love ghost stories\n* 🏙️ Anyone interested in Toronto's history\n* 🕯️ Fans of the strange and unexplained\n* 🤡 People brave enough to learn about Toronto's clown problem\n* 🚶 Anyone looking for something different to do in the evening\n* 😂 People who enjoy being a little creeped out without taking it too seriously\n\n***\n\n**Come for the history.**\n**Stay for the ghost stories.**\n**Leave looking at Old Toronto a little differently.** 👻🌙\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:** You're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email:\n📧 **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the history.**\n**Stay for the ghost stories.**\n**Leave looking at Old Toronto a little differently.** 👻🌙","startDate":"2026-10-29T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Fairmont Royal York","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"100 Front Street West, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"No Such Thing As Bad Weather Walking & Hiking Group!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/no-such-thing-as-bad-weather/"},"performer":"No Such Thing As Bad Weather Walking & Hiking Group!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"👻 Ghost Tour of Old Toronto  And Dinner🌙!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316201020/","description":"# 👻 Ghost Tour of Old Toronto 🌙\n\n### Haunted Hotels, Dark History & The Ghosts of Downtown\n\nToronto has a long history — and some of it is considerably darker than the history books make it sound.\n\nJoin us for an evening walk through **Old Toronto**, where we'll uncover stories of haunted hotels, gruesome executions, mysterious deaths, and some of the stranger legends that have become part of the city's history.\nWe'll walk through the downtown core as the city settles into the evening, stopping along the way for stories about the ghosts, tragedies, and unusual events connected to the streets and buildings around us.\nAnd yes, we'll even explore **why Toronto has a long-standing fear of clowns.** 🤡👻\n\nThis isn't simply a walk through downtown.\nIt's a **curated storytelling experience** that looks at some of Toronto's history from a decidedly darker perspective.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 👻 What We'll Explore\n\nWe'll begin outside the **Royal York Hotel** and make our way through Old Toronto toward the **Hockey Hall of Fame**.\nAlong the way, we'll hear stories about:\n\n* 🤡 **Why Toronto doesn't like clowns**\n* 🏨 **The ghosts of downtown's historic hotels**\n* 💀 **Gruesome executions and forgotten tragedies**\n* 🔫 **A deadly reminder of why you should never play with guns**\n* 👻 **Restless spirits and strange encounters**\n* 🕯️ And much, much more…\n\nWe'll remain outside throughout the experience and **will not be entering the buildings**.\n\n***\n\n## 🕯️ A Little About the Experience\n\nThis is one of our **curated ghost walks**, rather than a regular social walk.\nI've researched the stories, developed the route, and brought together some of the stranger pieces of Toronto's history to create an evening experience that is part history, part ghost story, and part “what the hell happened here?”\nYou don't have to believe in ghosts.\n**You just have to enjoy a good story.** 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** In front of the **Royal York Hotel**\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **6:30 PM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes**.\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🚶‍♂️ **Pace:** Steady walking pace\n🏁 **End Point:** **Hockey Hall of Fame**\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$10 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis is a **curated ghost-walking experience**, rather than one of our regular social walks. The route, stories, and history have been researched and brought together specifically for this experience.\nThe fee helps support the time and work that goes into creating these walks.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🧥 Weather-appropriate clothing\n💧 Water\n📱 Your phone for photos\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis experience is great for:\n\n* 👻 People who love ghost stories\n* 🏙️ Anyone interested in Toronto's history\n* 🕯️ Fans of the strange and unexplained\n* 🤡 People brave enough to learn about Toronto's clown problem\n* 🚶 Anyone looking for something different to do in the evening\n* 😂 People who enjoy being a little creeped out without taking it too seriously\n\n***\n\n**Come for the history.**\n**Stay for the ghost stories.**\n**Leave looking at Old Toronto a little differently.** 👻🌙\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:** You're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email:\n📧 **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the history.**\n**Stay for the ghost stories.**\n**Leave looking at Old Toronto a little differently.** 👻🌙","startDate":"2026-10-29T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Fairmont Royal York","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"100 Front St W, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Tech & Business Networking in  Toronto ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/startup-valley-toronto/events/316180265/","description":"📍 **Registration is on Luma — Meetup is not our RSVP platform.** Please register here to secure your spot: https://luma.com/0qzsvwty\n\n🚀 **Join our event in Toronto!**\n\nWe design Pitch and Networking nights to help founders sharpen their thinking through direct, candid feedback and to give strong investors access to serious teams.\n\n**Our pitch night is complemented by a structured networking session before and after the pitch session.**\n\n▶ **See how our pitch nights look:** https://vimeo.com/877496618\n\n**💡 What to expect:**\n\n- **Startups pitch live and receive focused feedback** from angels and VC partners\n- **Structured networking session** before and after the pitches\n- Entrepreneurs, startup founders, and operators are joining to network, exchange ideas, and build strong connections\n- Active investors and venture scouts joining to discover the best startups early\n\n**🤝 Who you will meet at the event:**\n\n- Founders\n- Investors, VC partners, Venture Scouts\n- Marketers, Salespeople, Business Advisors\n- Industry Disruptors\n- AI Experts\n- Entrepreneurs from Europe, Asia, and